From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] media: intel: ipu4: don't use vb2_v4l2_buffer.reserved

Intel's tree appends a "reserved" field to struct vb2_v4l2_buffer and the
isys stashes the CSI-2 index and VC in it. The field doesn't exist in the
stock struct, and only Intel's patched videobuf2 core ever copied it out to
user space, so against a stock kernel the stores are dead. Drop them.

---
--- a/ipu-isys-queue.c
+++ b/ipu-isys-queue.c
@@ -1296,15 +1296,6 @@
 		buf = to_vb2_v4l2_buffer(vb);
 		buf->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 
-		/*
-		 * Use "reserved" field to pass csi2 index and vc.
-		 * May need to change to other approach.
-		 */
-		buf->reserved &= 0xFFFFFF00;
-		if (ip->csi2)
-			buf->reserved |= ip->csi2->index << 4;
-		buf->reserved |= ip->vc;
-
 		list_del(&ib->head);
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&aq->lock, flags);
 
